  "exact_new_deduction": "At every fixed L,K>=3, the coherent projected outputs satisfy the exact index flow including the output normal scalar. The full discarded primitive covariance obeys X_K,c+q_V+C_K(V)=-gamma_L M A_e. This sums every finite Fourier tail, both parities and all native normals before estimating; there is no remaining separate R_K in this combined identity. It applies at Kd=ceil(L^4) without differentiating the cutoff.",
  "source_growth_price": "The whole Bbar_c+q_V+C_K is Delta_V and has the explicit source-fixed O((1+L)e^(Theta L)) bound. Individual pieces are not given that bound. No improvement of the unresolved Theta or all-positive-rate bound is proved.",
  "precise_failure_of_proposed_opposition": "The continuous two-direction mean-square law is exact, but restoring the complete pole cost cancels its apparent extra term. Keeping the early Arch W0 Jraw endpoint gives Bbar_c+q_V+C_K+Dpole=(W*W)(L), and the full Arch dictionary returns the original S(L-2c) with unit coefficient. This is a demonstrated equality, not a generic model counterexample or a claim that further arithmetic estimates are impossible.",
  "companion_implications": "The mean companion supplies a genuine eventual positive drift along L-c constant, where the potentially growing actual prime history is annihilated. Positive fixed-I mean energy retains rate 2Theta. Neither statement supplies an independently signed forcing for the complete echo equation.",
  "next_action_change": "Do not pursue a growing-order endpoint expansion solely to absorb the former separately estimated finite projection remainder. Preserve the exact joint cancellation and seek independent complete-source arithmetic information; geometric positivity, positive damping and boundary substitution do not currently provide it.",
